      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number [ⲕ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="9">The edition prints an opening bracket after ϥ . with three dots and no closing bracket (lost to the end of the line); it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="21">The letter after ⲙ in ⲙⲯⲩⲭⲁⲩⲉ is printed with arms curved up (ⲯ), unlike the straight-barred ϯ of ll. 5, 12 and 23.</p>
        <p n="22">Measured overline over ⲙⲛ of ⲛⲕⲉⲙⲛⲧⲛⲁⲉ (977–997): it covers ⲙ by 50 % and ⲛ by 57 %, so it is encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="24">The line ends with an opening bracket and nothing after it (lost to the end of the line).</p>
        <p n="25">The editors note that something is added above the line (apparatus); no text is printed for it.</p>
        <p n="32">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ inside the restoration. The edition opens a bracket before ⲟⲥ and does not close it (lost to the end of the line); it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="33">The edition prints a closing bracket after three dots with no opening bracket; the dots are encoded as illegible. The bracket before the last eight dots is not closed; it is closed here at the line end. So also l. 34 (seven dots).</p>
        <p n="35">The line is indented and begins with a closing bracket with no dots before it; the bracket before the last seven dots is not closed and is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="7">A short horizontal rule is printed in the right margin above the line end (x 1306–1376), after ⲡϣⲏ; it covers no letter by half and is not encoded.</p>
        <p n="8">The editors print "geringe Spuren" (slight traces) after the restoration; encoded as an inline note.</p>
        <p n="9">The editors print "ganz geringe Spuren" (very slight traces) before ϥ; encoded as an inline note.</p>
      </div>
